triage: fix_game: The rules are expressible on the platform, but the game does not put the expected options to the active player. In R8 seat 1 discarded a Guard and was never offered the number 3 (guard_guess defaulted to 2, so seat 2's Baron survived and no stake was paid). In R6 and R9 the options for the card to discard (ranks 1, 2, ...) were never offered.
step C: building the game file
triage: fix_game: Each attempt failed on a different coder-side slip: an unfillable {hand} placeholder in prompts, bookkeeping attributes left visible, and attributes that no step ever changes. None of these is a flaw in the rules or a missing engine capability. Hidden hands are supported, so the player's card only needs to come from state the player can see, not from prompt text.
